# Graph Sync Project

Project package: `__GRAPH_SYNC_PROJECT_PACKAGE__`

## Agent-Driven Workflow

Use the installed [Graph Sync Agent Kit](https://github.com/wordlift/graph-sync-agent-kit) with Codex or Claude Code for curation, implementation, validation, and publish handoff.

Codex prompt:

```text
Use the graph-sync-agent-kit:graph-sync-curator skill to continue the graph-sync workflow for this project.
```

Claude Code prompt:

```text
Use $graph-sync-curator to continue the graph-sync workflow for this project.
```

## Project Files

- `worai.toml`: graph-sync profile configuration.
- `profiles/`: profile-specific mappings, static templates, exports, and postprocessors.
- `.github/workflows/graph-sync.yml`: profile-based GitHub Actions workflow.
- `.env`: local secrets created during project generation and ignored by git.
- `docs/QUICKSTART.md`: short manual and agent-driven usage guide.
- `AGENTS.md`: project-specific agent notes and Graph Sync Agent Kit pointer.
- Runtime module: `acme_kg`

## Local Setup

```bash
uv sync
```

For local commands, load `.env` first:

```bash
set -a && source .env && set +a
```

## Maintenance

- `scripts/deploy_release.sh [major|minor|patch]`
- `scripts/upgrade_project.sh`
